   -X- System Outline

       Amber is a new and exciting development in the world of Amiga BBS
       systems. We have indulged a great deal of effort and thinking into
       the development of Amber BBS software. Amber is designed to be
       operable by even the very least skilled of computer operators. As
       long as you know how to use TYPE and the mouse, you can run Amber.

      ± Fully configurable!
      ± Multi-user, upto 16 lines
      ± Multi-tasking - you can use your Amiga AND run a BBS!
      ± Upto 256 file catalogues
      ± Upto 256 message areas
      ± Upto 40 sigs
      ± Unlimited menus, nested upto 8 levels deep
      ± Over 100 menu/door functions (menus and doors use the same commands)
      ± 7 different types of message base : Private, Local, Amiga+Net Echo or
        Netmail, UUCP or FidoNet Echo/Netmail
      ± Powerful event scheduler
      ± CoSysOp's supported
      ± Each file/message/sig area can have a Section SysOp
      ± Powerful inter-user communication/pageing/mailing system
      ± Supports upto 56.7bps!
      ± Works with ANY modem!

   -X- Features

       Unlike some BBS packages, Amber isn't a one-man, or solo project.
       It's progress has been carefully monitored, controlled and aided
       by a team of five, experienced sysops, working together as a
       development team, in conjunction with the two core programmers.
       Many of the fine ideas chosen for implementation within the Amber
       system were discovered or produced by the development team...

      ± FULL Intuition interface locally!
       ¯ AmCon (controller) is intuition based!
       ¯ Detailed status screen lists activity on all lines.
       ¯ Intuition based user editor built into AmCon (can edit users online)
       ¯ Intuition based configurator!
       ¯ Intuition based menu editor!
      ± Amber is the first BBS package in the world to feature Amiga+Net.
        See below for details of Amiga+Net
      ± Built in Amiga+Net Mailer
      ± Compatible with ANY standard Amiga+Net message reader/writer.
      ± Support for FidoNet message areas, FidoNet mailers etc.
      ± Support for external front ends.
      ± Built in online conference system
      ± _3_ built in pagers
      ± Users can page co-sysops/section sysops.
      ± Feedback gives option to leave mail to CoSysOp's/Section SysOps.
      ± Built in private user<->user chat booth, allow users to communicate
        directly, like a chat mode. "Monitor" can be disabled to allow users
        to transfer files using your system as a satellite!
      ± Multi-user sysop chat (windowed if users have ansi enabled)
      ± Option to upload pre-prepared message text at message entry.
      ± 1xLocal line, 15xModem lines.
      ± Built in "door interpretor" to aid door development.
      ± "Hidden login" facility for sysops.
      ± "Forced Logon" or "Logon from voice" facility.
      ± "Leave message to next caller" option.
       ¯ Configurable by access level. All messages logged.
      ± At logon user can specify "reason for call"
       ¯ Configurable by access level. All reasons logged.
      ± At logoff, users can leave a "hardcopy message" if you have a printer
        so you can check for urgent messages WITHOUT touching the computer!
       ¯ Configurable by access level.
      ± Active lines can be hidden/recalled at a single mouse click!
      ± Password for sysop functions (protect your board from those crazy
        friends who want extra access!)
      ± Password for DOS gate.
      ± Each line can have different modem result codes, and SysOp can
        define different connect strings for each code/speed!
      ± Speed locking supported!
      ± System warnings/errors/reports are posted in messages to a special
        account, "Operator" which can be read by SysOp/CoSysop/Section SysOps.
        This avoids your BBS telling users to "Inform the SysOp" and means
        that any "online" sysop will be made aware of the problem until the
        message is deleted!
      ± Amber conforms to the standard Amiga+Net message structure. See below
      ± Each file area can have a "catalog header". This is displayed each
        time the user calls up a list of files from that area.
      ± Files can be set to "Free download", allowing users to download
        without affecting up/download ratio (such as archivers).
      ± Users exceeding u/d ratio cannot download FREE downloads.
      ± Open/Closed uploads. In Closed mode, files must be validated by SysOp
        before users can download them.
      ± SysOp is informed via a message of new user applications and new
        uploads. System uses same message until (a) it is deleted, (b) it
        is received or (c) the system reboots.
      ± Amber uses external protocols so your transfer options are always
        upto date! This also reduces code size!
      ± Built in terminal program with up/download and capture facilities!
      ± SysOp can login "quietly" without being listed to other users online,
        ESSENTIAL for a quick check on the board, or to quickly leave a
        message to someone, without getting paged...

   -X- Amiga+Net Features

      ± Standard message format uses a fixed size header, with variable sized
        text fields, and a variable sized expansion space, allowing message
        format to be used anywhere! And also allowing future expansion with
        great ease!
      ± Message format bonuses:
       ¯ Future expansion made EASILY possible, without causing problems
          with existing software.
       ¯ Upto 2560 files attached to one message!
       ¯ Attached file names upto 256 characters long!
       ¯ Virtually unlimited replies to a message.
       ¯ Smooth, fast and efficient message threading.
       ¯ "Expiry date" causes messages to be AUTOMATICALLY deleted after
          becoming obsolete, such as adverts for computer shows etc.
       ¯ Only one copy of a message required for carbon copying!
      ± No need for message upload/download utilities anymore! SysOp can
        allow users to act as "points" of his system, using net number 65535
        (-1) and the users ID number as the node number.
      ± Amiga+Net system allows "intelligent comms software" to exchange
        "point mail".
      ± Amiga+Net allows automatic login by intelligent software.
      ± Amiga+Net allows transparent registration - near instantaneous!

