   -X- Third Party Support

       The outsider was always in our mind whilst developing Amber. A great
       deal of effort has been concentrated in saving development time of
       external utilities and applications. Using the standard AmigaDOS
       communications port system, Amber exposes itself to the probings of
       the external <thing>. This reduces time wasted on rewriting routines
       and space wasted in duplicating them! It also means that non-assembler
       programs have access to highly optimized, and very efficient 68000
       coded routines.

      ± ** All literature duplicated to cater for 68000 AND 'C' **
      ± Full doccumentation for doors programming available. (C/ASM)
      ± Full doccumentatino for application programming available. (C/ASM)
      ± Includes/linkables for assembler AND 'C' available.
      ± AmCon, the system controller, makes the most of the essential
        BBS Database accessible to third partys with minimum effort!
      ± Amber makes many of its internal routines accessible to the third
        party to reduce development time of external programs wasted in
        the re-writing of commonly used functions! This also reduces the
        size of external programs, and even Amber!
      ± Many of the functions vital for automation of external programs are
        accessible through the message port command system.
      ± Amber uses external protocols for file transfers, so any new protocol
        that is released on the Amiga can be used with Amber BBS!

   -X- Miscellaneous

      ± No "Naughty-hacks" involved in Amber! Amber is 100% O/S friendly.
      ± Configurable PAL/NTSC and COLOR/MONO screen.
      ± Amber makes use of the ARP library... Not for DOS functions, but
        for the bonus programming routines, such as string formatting,
        date stamp conversion, text processing etc. These are normally
        linked into 'C' programs increasing the size.
      ± Amber makes use of the InovaTronics "InovaTools1" library, saving
        memory usage on the intuition functions featured regularily in
        Amber/AmCon/Config/MenuAuthor!
      ± Amber can be used in conjunction with TrapDoor and other such
        external front ends, to allow compatibility with FidoNet or other
        popular mail networks.

